# A mirror, and it is honest about being one.
#
# Docker reads the ignore file at the root of the BUILD CONTEXT. `web/Dockerfile`
# is built with the repository root as its context — it has to be, because the
# image carries `engine/` and `bin/report-maker` — so the file that actually
# governs that build is `/.dockerignore`, one level up. Keep the two in step.
#
# This file matters when somebody builds with `web/` as the context:
#
#     docker build -f Dockerfile -t something .      # run from inside web/
#
# which cannot produce the image this repository ships (the engine is not in
# that context), but which is exactly the mistake that otherwise uploads
# `client/node_modules` — a few hundred megabytes — before failing.

# Generated, and rebuilt inside the image anyway.
client/node_modules/
client/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store

# Not code the server runs.
tests/
README.md
fly.toml
render.yaml
Dockerfile
